From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3: drive touch mode-select gpio174 low

The Himax HX83121A cascade TDDI controller selects its host transport at
firmware reload time by sampling GPIO 174:
- GPIO 174 low at reload selects SPI raw-data mode (used by himax-spi);
- GPIO 174 high at reload selects I2C HID mode (used by UEFI firmware).

Because the device tree did not configure GPIO 174, the pin remained at the
high level left by UEFI, causing the controller to latch into I2C mode across
touch or panel resets and leaving himax-spi without touch events. Drive
GPIO 174 low in the touchscreen default pinctrl state before driver probe and
firmware reload.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-huawei-gaokun3.dts
@@ -1658,6 +1658,12 @@
 	};

 	ts0_default: ts0-default-state {
+		mode-pins {
+			pins = "gpio174";
+			function = "gpio";
+			output-low;
+		};
+
 		int-n-pins {
 			pins = "gpio175";
 			function = "gpio";
